# random: eight knobs, a per-pattern note pool picked on the piano, in-scale dots; steps as active slots; no format bump
wait 300
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
knob 2 player rand
expect par2.player 4
tap ARP
expect page Players
shot random_players.png
turn SELECT 1
expect page Players_2
shot random_players2.png
turn SELECT 1
expect page Players_3
# the octave knobs on page 3: oct down 1 and oct up 2 (the step's own octave, a note one below to two above)
knob 2 p4 1
expect par2.p4 1
knob 2 octup 2
expect par2.octup 2
wait 40
shot random_players3.png
# the pool picker: hold a step, SEQ; the keys toggle C and E
tap SEQ
key w0 down
tap SEQ
key w0 up
tapkey w4
tapkey w6
expect pool 2 1 0x11
shot random_pool.png
tap SEQ
# the follow mode's notes are dotted under their keys, whether or not the pool holds them (C major here)
knob 2 brain diatonic
tap SEQ
key w0 down
tap SEQ
key w0 up
shot random_pool_dots.png
tap SEQ
# harmony: the dots shrink to the conductor's chord (D minor: D F A), held on its keys
knob 2 brain harmony
play 9 62 on
play 9 65 on
play 9 69 on
tap SEQ
key w0 down
tap SEQ
key w0 up
shot random_pool_chord.png
tap SEQ
play 9 62 off
play 9 65 off
play 9 69 off
knob 2 brain diatonic
# steps as active slots: tap two on (with none set, every step plays)
tapkey w0
tapkey w2
shot random_slots.png
# a slot's note sets the register, and the cell shows only that octave, its pitch drawn: C2 is *2, C5 is *5
notes 2 1 1 1 100 C2
notes 2 1 3 1 100 C5
wait 40
shot random_octaves.png
# play a phrase and save it (the pool lives in a lane: no project format change)
tap PLAY
wait 1200
shot random_playing.png
tap PLAY
projsave 1
reboot
wait 400
expect pool 2 1 0x11
# leaving random frees the pool's lane (the lanes are shared by the whole project: nothing taken that no page shows)
knob 2 player arp
expect par2.player 1
expect pool 2 1 0x000
